# Public projection consumer rules

- Consume only `professional-public-projection/v1` already present in this repo.
- Never read, clone, mount, query or fetch the private source during build,
  tests, preview or deploy.
- Reject unknown versions, unknown fields and private/internal material through
  the closed public schema.
- Treat the projection as finished public content for the actual site and CV,
  not as a fact registry or editorial workflow.
- Site and CV content are independent in selection and wording. `cv` is required
  and must be complete.
- Do not add approval actors, publication permissions, editorial states,
  fact-to-copy joins or symmetry requirements.
- Keep professional copy in the projection and presentation concerns in Astro;
  do not maintain duplicate professional copy in page components.
- Make schema/load error behavior consistent and contextual.
- Generic helpers may accept test paths, but production entry points must use
  explicit repository-local files. Document the actual guarantee, not a stronger
  one.
- The closed schema is the allowlist. Do not add a redundant private-key walker
  unless it protects a distinct demonstrated risk.
- Technical validity never authorizes publishing, deployment or repository
  visibility.
